From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Winios: post a key extended for the host app

winios_post_key carries a virtual key only, so the host could not post
keypad Enter: it went out as VK_RETURN with scan 0x1C and no E0, the
main Return key to a game reading scan codes or WM_KEYDOWN's extended
bit.

winios_post_key_extended queues the key with KEYEVENTF_EXTENDEDKEY.
The drain already hands an event's flags to win32u's
winios_drv_post_key, which keeps the flag and takes the scan code from
its map as before (0x1C for VK_RETURN), so the game sees E0 1C.

Linear: PLA-599
Class: host-app
Evidence: app/HostIOKit/Tests/HostIOKitTests (KeyMap marks keypad Enter extended; phone gate not run)
Offered-upstream: no; the extended key feeds the iOS app's keyboard path
---
 app/Madeira/Winios/Winios.m | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/Madeira/Winios/Winios.m b/app/Madeira/Winios/Winios.m
index bdd4e0e..ab15c02 100644
--- a/app/Madeira/Winios/Winios.m
+++ b/app/Madeira/Winios/Winios.m
@@ -512,6 +512,13 @@ void winios_post_key(int vk, int down) {
     winios_q_push_ev(WINIOS_EV_KEY, vk, 0, down ? 0 : KEYEVENTF_KEYUP, 0);
 }
 
+/* Playport (app HostIO): a key its virtual key cannot tell from another,
+ * posted with KEYEVENTF_EXTENDEDKEY (0x0001), which win32u's
+ * winios_drv_post_key keeps: keypad Enter is VK_RETURN with E0. */
+void winios_post_key_extended(int vk, int down) {
+    winios_q_push_ev(WINIOS_EV_KEY, vk, 0, 0x0001 | (down ? 0 : KEYEVENTF_KEYUP), 0);
+}
+
 /* Playport (app HostIO): two event kinds the host posts that only a
  * Wine thread can resolve, so they are converted here, in the drain, which runs
  * on the guest thread that is pumping its messages.
